# Declarative schema (current SQL)

`supabase/schemas/` is the **current** public schema (`_extensions.sql` + `public.sql`). `supabase/migrations/` holds `00000000000000_baseline.sql` plus generated deltas; `_legacy/` is archived imperative history.

How-to: [doc/supabase-schema.md](../../doc/supabase-schema.md)

## Edit

- Change tables / functions / policies in `supabase/schemas/public.sql` (or re-split domains per `schema-split` skill), not via hand-written DDL migrations.
- Generate migrations: `pnpm run backend:schema:sync -- <name>` (`declarative sync --no-apply`). Review SQL before `backend:local` or deploy.
- Split: user says `split schema <domain>` — follow `.agents/skills/schema-split/SKILL.md`. Update `schema_paths` in `config.toml`; do not leave duplicate DDL under `schemas/` (pg-delta scans all `*.sql` there).
- Keep `supabase/schemas/_extensions.sql`; baseline migration also includes extensions omitted from `pg_dump`.

## Do not use db diff for declarative work

- Use `backend:schema:sync`, not `supabase db diff -f`, for schema DDL.
- Hand-write migrations for **DML only** (seeds, backfills, permission **rows**). Diff cannot see data.
- Do not edit already-applied migration files for features.
- Do not `db reset` or experimental `db diff` against production. Production only gets `pnpm run deploy:backend`.
